# infra/apps/<% app.name %> — <% project.name %> (<% derived.env %>, compute: Azure Container Apps)

Generated by slipway from `templates/compute/aca/per-app/infra/apps`. Owns exactly one container app, `<% app.name %>`, in the shared
environment `cae-<% project.name %>-<% derived.env %>` (created by `infra/foundation`), pulling `<% app.image %>:<image_tag>` with the identity `<% azure.identity_name %>`.
Other apps have their own root module and state, so deploying `<% app.name %>` never plans another app's image.

| Command | Who |
|---|---|
| `/slipway:plan <% derived.env %> --layer apps/<% app.name %> --image-tag <tag>` | anyone; read-only |
| `/slipway:deploy <% app.name %> <tag> <% derived.env %>` | triggers `<% app.workflow_cd %>`: plan job, then apply behind the `<% github.cd_environment %>` environment approval |

Never apply this layer from a laptop: the guard hook blocks it and the state key (`<% app.state_key %>`) is written by the CD identity.
